@nsobid-7E1DF8E08D60544BBDCA1E333C153C97

# Xenoblade Chronicles: Definitive Edition 2.0.0 - 3840x2160 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 3840x2160 instead of the stock 1280x720 or less. The game uses
// the same size docked and handheld, so the mod holds in both modes.
//
// The engine sizes the frame from the NVN window textures: two color buffers
// and a depth buffer created at 1280x720 on one pair of registers. The scene
// targets take the window texture size, and the render-target planner lays out
// every G-buffer, depth, post-process, TMAA and bloom target in one GPU pool
// from the device size getters, both when it is built and when it is
// re-planned. Both now use 3840x2160; the planner's half, quarter and mip
// sizes follow from it, and so do the pool offsets.
//
// The device size getters stay at 1280x720. The game calls them for work laid
// out in that space, such as debug overlays and camera aspect ratios.
//
// The UI layer maps layout units to the screen with twice the canvas scale,
// min(width/1280, height/720), which is 1 at stock. Layout part panes, such as
// the title menu, place their child panes from offsets in 1280x720 layout
// pixels, but first divide them by width/1280 as if they were screen pixels.
// That factor is 1 at stock and nothing else reads it; at a higher resolution
// the children slide toward the top-left corner while keeping their size. The
// divisor is pinned to 1.0.
//
// The layer's size getters return the render target size, but every caller
// in the game UI treats it as the 1280x720 layout size: screen centers for
// menus, maps and cursors, and clamp bounds for pane positions. They return
// the layout size instead, which is what they return at stock.
//
// Nine-slice window and stretch panes size their corner and edge pieces from
// the pane size in layout pixels, but divide that size by the canvas scale
// once more. At stock the scale is 1; at a higher resolution the pieces grow
// by the scale, which enlarges the frame corners and pulls the frame inside
// the window. Both divisors are pinned to 1.0.
//
// The graphics device caches the current viewport and seeds it with
// 1280x720 before the first frame sets one; the seed is the full target.
//
// Dynamic resolution steps the frame between 0.94 x 1.0 and 0.6 x 0.84 of the
// window size based on GPU load, so stock docked output tops out at about
// 1203x720. Its default scales come from a read-only table; the minimum,
// maximum and starting scales are set to 1.0, so every level renders the full
// 3840x2160.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 8 GiB or higher. Every render
// target comes from the GLIBPXL texture heap (350 MB) inside GLIBTOP (489 MB),
// carved from the 512 MB MLGRAHANDLE root heap. The larger targets need about
// 2560 MB more, so GLIBPXL and MLGRAHANDLE each grow by exactly that much and
// the parent keeps its stock headroom: 2910 MB GLIBPXL, 3049 MB GLIBTOP,
// 3072 MB MLGRAHANDLE. The root heaps are malloc'd from
// nn::os::SetMemoryHeapSize(all remaining memory), which follows the
// emulator's DRAM setting.
@enabled
// Window textures (both color buffers and the depth buffer).
00612548 15E08152   // MOV W21, #0xF00 = width (was MOV W21,#0x500)
0061254C 160E8152   // MOV W22, #0x870 = height (was MOV W22,#0x2D0)
// Initial cached viewport rectangle.
009D1F68 0000704500000745   // 3840.0, 2160.0 (was 1280.0, 720.0)
// Render-target planner base size (was the 1280x720 device getters).
006A1E34 00E08152   // MOV W0, #0xF00 = build width (was BL 0x5B5F40)
006A1E3C 000E8152   // MOV W0, #0x870 = build height (was BL 0x5B5F60)
006A1EB0 00E08152   // MOV W0, #0xF00 = re-plan width (was BL 0x5B5F40)
006A1EB8 000E8152   // MOV W0, #0x870 = re-plan height (was BL 0x5B5F60)
// Layer size getters return the 1280x720 layout size.
00749894 00D145BD   // LDR S0, [X8, #0x5D0] = layout width (was LDR S0,[X8,#0x5B0])
007498A4 00D545BD   // LDR S0, [X8, #0x5D4] = layout height (was LDR S0,[X8,#0x5B4])
// Layout part child placement: offsets are already in layout pixels.
0075EB9C 03102E1E   // FMOV S3, #1.00000000 = width/1280 divisor (was LDR S3,[X9,#0x5DC])
// Nine-slice piece sizes: pane size is already in layout pixels.
00753048 01102E1E   // FMOV S1, #1.00000000 = stretch pane scale (was FDIV S1,S4,S1)
00753F3C 00102E1E   // FMOV S0, #1.00000000 = window pane scale (was FDIV S0,S1,S0)
// Dynamic resolution defaults: max, min and starting scales all 1.0.
009D360C 0000803F   // max x 1.0 (was 0.94)
009D3614 0000803F   // min x 1.0 (was 0.6)
009D3618 0000803F   // min y 1.0 (was 0.84)
009D361C 0000803F   // starting x 1.0 (was 0.94)
// GPU memory: GLIBPXL and its MLGRAHANDLE root grow by the same amount.
009D1F44 0000E0B5   // GLIBPXL 2910 MB (was 350 MB)
00009858 0800B852   // MOV W8, #0xC0000000 = MLGRAHANDLE 3072 MB (was ORR W8,WZR,#0x20000000, 512 MB)
@stop

